# The Execution Squad. API keys.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the real values.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# During /setup, Claude asks for each of these one at a time, with a direct
# link to where you create the key. Claude writes the values into .env
# for you. You never have to touch this file by hand unless you want to.
#
# .env is gitignored. You will never accidentally commit it.

# === Research + Scraping ===
# Perplexity: research and competitor analysis
# Get yours: https://www.perplexity.ai/settings/api
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=

# Apify: scrape Reddit, YouTube, LinkedIn, Apollo
# Get yours: https://console.apify.com/account/integrations
APIFY_TOKEN=

# === Cold Outreach (Day 21 onward) ===
# Instantly: cold email campaigns
# Get yours: https://app.instantly.ai/app/settings/integrations
INSTANTLY_API_KEY=

# Supabase: outreach dashboard database (free tier works)
# Create a project: https://supabase.com/dashboard
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# === YouTube (Month 3 onward) ===
# YouTube Data API key for quota. OAuth runs in-browser the first time
# a /youtube command needs it.
# Get yours: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# === Warm Outreach + Scheduling (Day 4 onward) ===
# Gmail uses OAuth, so there is no key to paste. A browser window
# opens the first time the warm DM Skill sends an email.

# Cal.com: booking calls with prospects
# Get yours: https://app.cal.com/settings/developer/api-keys
CAL_API_KEY=

# === Payments (add after your first client closes) ===
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
